# What the public build actually needs: site/content, the console source, and
# scripts/build_public.py. Everything else is either the product itself or local
# state — shipping it to a build container is slower and a wider surface than the
# deployment needs.
#
# NOTE: patterns here match at ANY depth, .gitignore-style. A bare `*.md` would
# therefore exclude site/content/**/*.md — the entire source of the site — and
# produce an empty build. Directories are named explicitly instead.

# The Python package is not needed to build the site: site/facts.json is
# committed, and CI fails if it goes stale. Shipping ~1 MB of product source to a
# static-site build container would widen the surface for nothing.
atheros-compliance-kit/
services/
artifacts/
.github/
.atheros/

console/node_modules/
console/dist/
site/dist/
public/
.vercel/

BRAND_KIT.md
CHANGELOG.md
PLAYBOOK.md
RELEASING.md
SELF_ASSESSMENT.md
